Subject: [PATCH] zero: poll for safepoints on backward branches

Source:  manga_backup_converter source runners (U16), original work
Licence: GPLv2 (same as the patched OpenJDK file)

Restores a back-edge safepoint/handshake poll in the Zero bytecode
interpreter (JDK 11 Zero polled on back-edges; current Zero leaves
DO_BACKEDGE_CHECKS empty). Without it a call-free Java loop blocks GC and
handshakes for all threads, and JVMTI StopThread (delivered by handshake)
cannot reach the looping thread. KTD11 interruption mechanism B.
---
--- a/src/hotspot/share/interpreter/zero/bytecodeInterpreter.cpp	2026-11-20 09:28:05
+++ b/src/hotspot/share/interpreter/zero/bytecodeInterpreter.cpp	2026-11-20 09:28:05
@@ -302,7 +302,17 @@
 
 #define METHOD istate->method()
 #define GET_METHOD_COUNTERS(res)
-#define DO_BACKEDGE_CHECKS(skip, branch_pc)
+// source-runner patch: poll for safepoints and handshakes on backward
+// branches. Upstream Zero polls only at method return, so a call-free loop
+// stalls GC and handshakes (including JVMTI StopThread delivery) for every
+// other thread. The embedder may clear this switch to measure the unpatched
+// behaviour; production builds leave it set.
+extern "C" JNIEXPORT volatile int source_runner_zero_backedge_poll = 1;
+#define DO_BACKEDGE_CHECKS(skip, branch_pc)                                  \
+    if ((skip) <= 0 && source_runner_zero_backedge_poll != 0 &&              \
+        SafepointMechanism::should_process(THREAD)) {                        \
+      CALL_VM(at_safepoint(THREAD), handle_exception);                       \
+    }
 
 /*
  * For those opcodes that need to have a GC point on a backwards branch
